==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|lernere}}, from {{inh|en|ang|leornere}}. {{surf|+suf|en|learn|er}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈlɜɹnəɹ/|a=UK,US}}
** {{IPA|en|[ˈlɝ.nɚ]|a=US}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈlɜːnə/|a=RP}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɜː(ɹ)nə(ɹ)|s=2}}
* {{hyphenation|en|learn|er}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-I learned some phrases-learner.wav|a=UK}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# One who is [[learn]]ing; one [[receive|receiving]] [[instruction]].
#: {{ux|en|She’s still a '''learner''', so she’s prone to making mistakes.}}
#: {{ux|en|Cambridge University Press has released a new series aimed at young '''learners''' with epilepsy.}}
# {{lb|en|dated|obsolete}} A [[scholar]].

